2026-07-22T16:11:17.1003698Z     The ``pytest`` framework makes it easy to write small tests, yet
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1004156Z     scales to support complex functional testing for applications and libraries.
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1004531Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1004726Z     An example of a simple test:
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1004965Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005162Z     .. code-block:: python
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005238Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005347Z         # content of test_sample.py
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005436Z         def inc(x):
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005531Z             return x + 1
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005613Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005864Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1005966Z         def test_answer():
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006067Z             assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006143Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006225Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006321Z     To execute it::
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006398Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006488Z         $ pytest
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006658Z         ============================= test session starts =============================
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006749Z         collected 1 items
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006832Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1006931Z         test_sample.py F
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007007Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007150Z         ================================== FAILURES ===================================
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007315Z         _________________________________ test_answer _________________________________
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007515Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007614Z             def test_answer():
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007713Z         >       assert inc(3) == 5
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007809Z         E       assert 4 == 5
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007908Z         E        +  where 4 = inc(3)
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1007988Z     
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1008095Z         test_sample.py:5: AssertionError
2026-07-22T16:11:17.1008249Z         ========================== 1 failed in 0.04 seconds ===========================
